From fa698ccbcd9bbe2ea0747ec9bfb8857c1eda1b8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:50:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] VideoOutput: rotate camera frames by the camera
 orientation (default renderer), Release 8

jolla-camera never sets VideoOutput.orientation: on hybris the video texture
backend rotates the viewfinder by the image-orientation tag droidcamsrc puts
on its viewfinder stream. Qt's own renderer ignores that tag, and libcamerasrc
sends none, so the viewfinder showed raw landscape sensor frames (Pro1-X:
90 degrees counter-clockwise).

With the default renderer backend and autoOrientation off, the camera's
QCameraInfo::orientation is now added to the orientation used for
rendering, geometry and point/rect mapping (renderOrientation()). The
orientation property keeps the value the application set. The texture
backend and autoOrientation are unchanged.

Contract change for this renderer: an application that compensates the
camera orientation itself by setting VideoOutput.orientation now rotates
twice. jolla-camera does not. Front cameras are not mirrored here (the
texture backend mirrors them).

LLMGD-0 A0
